# Usage: activescrubs [-s COLUMN] [-r] [-t TYPE] [-i SECONDS]
#
# Show the pgs that are active scrubbing with automatic period updates.
#
# Command line options:
#   -s, --sort COLUMN   Column to sort the display by.  One of:
#                       pgid, type, objects, scrubbed, rate, percent.
#   -r, --reverse       Sort in descending order.
#   -t, --type TYPE     Scrub types to show: shallow, deep or both.
#   -i, --interval SEC  Seconds between refreshes.
#
# Interactive keys:
#   q        Quit.
#   <space>  Refresh now.
#   s <key>  Sort by a column: p=PGID, t=Type, o=Objects, c=Scrubbed count,
#            r=Obj/s rate, %=Percent.
#   r        Toggle ascending / descending sort.
#   t        Cycle the scrub type filter (both -> shallow -> deep).
#   + / -    Increase / decrease the refresh interval by INTERVAL_STEP seconds.
#
# Things to do:
